  "gaps": [
    "Individual core and specialization course credits are printed in a detached column in the two-column PDF capture; values were assigned by column order (BUS2003/BUS2007 6, BUS1011 3, BUS2012 3, BUS2021 3, BUS2030 6, BUS2061 3, BUS2062 3, BUS3022 3, BUS3040 6, BUS3050 6; each specialization course 6). These are consistent with the stated block minimums (core 42, specialization 48) but should be verified against the source.",
    "Credits for the specialization option courses BUS4024, BUS4027 and BUS4035 are not printed adjacent to the titles; only the 12-quarter-credit block amount is used.",
    "The capture does not state explicitly whether MAT2010 Practical Statistics counts within the 45 general education quarter credits. The block totals (45 + 42 + 48 + 39 + 6 = 180) imply it does, so it should not be added on top of the 45.",
    "ACS1003 is required only for students determined by academic assessment to need additional support (taken in the first quarter). The capture does not say whether its 6 credits count toward the 39 elective credits or are added to the 180 total.",
    "The footnotes marked ‡ (core courses) and § (elective courses) are not included in the capture.",
    "The degree requires a minimum of 54 quarter credits from the 3000-level and above; this constraint is not represented as a separate ledger line.",
    "The capture does not state residency or institutional-credit requirements (courses that must be completed at Capella).",
    "The optional Honors Pathway (PHI-H2005 3, COM-H4005 6, SOC-H3005 6; at least 15 quarter credits applied toward general education) is not listed as a separate requirement because it applies only to honors-pathway students.",
    "The general education category list is only partially captured: the credit pairing for individual Communication, Humanities and Natural Science courses is garbled in the two-column layout. The category minimums (4 quarter credits each) are stated, but category assignment per course should be confirmed from p. 148.",
    "Prerequisites are referenced ('Refer to the course descriptions') but are not included in the capture."
  ],
